      "created_at": "2025-09-25T04:10:01.025Z",
      "cooked": "<p><strong>Problem statement</strong></p>\n<p>Users often update <strong>master data</strong> (e.g., customer name, billing/shipping address, item name/description) while transactions (quotations, sales orders, invoices, delivery notes, etc.) are being created or after they’ve been submitted.</p>\n<p><strong>Question</strong></p>\n<p>When master data changes, which values should forms use?</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A. Latest master data</strong> — always pull current values at render</li>\n<li><strong>B. Document snapshot</strong> — use values saved on the document; never auto-refresh after submit</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Thank you.</p>",
